{"chunk_id": "3852e384dc4b", "text": "Rama arrives at the royal palace amid the joy and admiration of Ayodhya\u2019s people, moving serenely through the sacred spaces and into the king\u2019s private chambers. There he finds King Dasaratha pale, anguished, and unable to speak, seated beside Queen Kaikeyi. Disturbed by his father\u2019s condition, Rama humbly asks the cause and declares his absolute obedience to his father\u2019s will, even to the point of death. Kaikeyi, cold and calculating, reveals the truth: long ago the king granted her two boons, and she now claims them\u2014Bharata must be crowned king and Rama must go into exile in the Dandaka forest for fourteen years. Rama receives the decree without visible distress, while Dasaratha, foreseeing his son\u2019s suffering, is crushed by grief. The moment marks the decisive turning point that sends Rama into exile and sets the epic\u2019s central journey in motion.\nRama visits Dasharatha, sees his distress, and Kaikeyi reveals her demand: Bharata\u2019s coronation and Rama\u2019s fourteen\u2011year exile to honor the king\u2019s old promise.\nThemes: filial duty, truth and vows, royal intrigue, exile, parental anguish", "vector": [0.014367078430950642, -0.02276548184454441, -0.017219366505742073, -0.0063780322670936584, -0.019332172349095345, 0.006820400711148977, -0.027545703575015068, -0.019503837451338768, -0.018553074449300766, 0.004578846041113138, 0.007929624058306217, 0.0007972540333867073, -0.012696641497313976, 0.02714955247938633, -0.018619099631905556, 0.00338379037566483, 0.04349738731980324, -0.019451016560196877, 0.02585545927286148, -0.002796166343614459, 0.005182976368814707, -0.006328513380140066, 0.001114174840040505, 0.02065267600119114, -0.020230114459991455, -0.004067150875926018, 0.020243318751454353, -0.03137516230344772, 0.024138804525136948, -0.026264814659953117, -0.010174479335546494, -0.008702117949724197, 0.011263894848525524, -0.008055071346461773, -0.026278020814061165, 0.015978